<div class="relative overflow-x-clip bg-night text-ink font-body leading-[1.58] antialiased selection:bg-ember selection:text-[#160c02]">
  <div class="v2-ambient" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="relative z-[1]">

    {# ---------- hero ---------- #}
    <header class="pt-10 pb-[clamp(40px,5vw,60px)]" style="--acc:var(--color-flame)">
    <div class="max-w-[1140px] mx-auto px-7">
      <p class="mb-[26px] font-smono text-[.7rem] tracking-[.08em] text-ink-3"><a class="hover:text-spark" href="/">Bonfire</a><span class="mx-2">/</span>Compare</p>
      <p class="{{ eyebrow }}"><i class="w-[9px] h-[9px] flex-none bg-[var(--acc)] [clip-path:polygon(50%_0,100%_50%,50%_100%,0_50%)]" aria-hidden="true"></i>How Bonfire compares</p>
      <h1 class="mt-[22px] font-disp font-semibold text-[clamp(2.1rem,5vw,3.7rem)] leading-[1.05] tracking-[-.02em] text-balance max-w-[20ch] [font-variation-settings:'opsz'_96]">Give your community <span class="fire-text">a world of its own.</span></h1>
      <p class="mt-[42px] text-[1.08rem] text-ink-2 max-w-[58ch] [&_b]:text-ink [&_b]:font-semibold">Most community tools are a room you rent inside someone else's building: you pay per member, live on their domain, and leave with only what they let you export. Bonfire is <b>open source, self-hostable and federated</b>: a space that's yours, connected to the whole open social web. Here's how they compare.</p>
    </div>
    </header>

    <main>

    {# ---------- the table ---------- #}
    <section class="py-[clamp(40px,5vw,64px)] border-t border-ink/[0.07]" style="--acc:var(--color-flame)">
    <div class="max-w-[1140px] mx-auto px-7">

      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-5 gap-y-2 mb-5 font-smono text-[.68rem] text-ink-3">
        <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5"><span class="icon-[ph--check-bold] text-leaf" aria-hidden="true"></span> yes</span>
        <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5"><span class="icon-[ph--minus-bold] text-corn-2" aria-hidden="true"></span> partial / limited</span>
        <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5"><span class="icon-[ph--x-bold] text-ink-3/50" aria-hidden="true"></span> no</span>
        <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5"><span class="icon-[ph--clock-bold] text-flame" aria-hidden="true"></span> coming</span>
        <span class="ml-auto max-[640px]:ml-0">scroll right · hover for detail →</span>
      </div>

      <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-ink/15 [scrollbar-width:thin]">
        <table class="border-collapse text-left">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th class="sticky left-0 z-[4] bg-night-2 w-[150px] min-w-[150px]"></th>
              {%- for g in groups %}
              <th colspan="{{ g.rows | length }}" class="px-2 py-2 text-center font-smono text-[.54rem] font-bold tracking-[.1em] uppercase border-b border-b-ink/[0.07] border-l border-l-ink/20 {{ stickyBonfire if g.rows[0].bonfire else 'bg-night-2 text-ink-3' }} {{ 'text-flame' if g.rows[0].bonfire }}">{{ g.cat }}</th>
              {%- endfor %}
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <th class="sticky left-0 z-[4] bg-night-2 w-[150px] min-w-[150px] px-4 py-2 border-b border-ink/15 align-bottom font-smono text-[.6rem] font-bold tracking-[.1em] uppercase text-ink-3">Platform</th>
              {%- for g in groups %}{%- for r in g.rows %}
              <th title="{{ r.name }}" style="min-width: {{ '112px' if platformHeaderStyle == 'names' else '80px' }}" class="px-2 py-3 align-bottom text-center border-b border-b-ink/[0.07] {{ 'border-l border-l-ink/20' if loop.first }} {{ stickyBonfire if r.bonfire else 'bg-night-2' }}">
                {%- if platformHeaderStyle == "names" and r.bonfire -%}
                  <img src="{{ r.logoImg }}" alt="{{ r.name }}" class="h-6 mx-auto object-contain" loading="lazy">
                {%- elif platformHeaderStyle == "names" -%}
                  <span class="block max-w-[15ch] mx-auto font-disp font-[620] text-[.74rem] leading-[1.15] text-balance {{ 'text-flame' if r.bonfire else 'text-ink' }}">{{ r.name }}</span>
                {%- elif r.logoImg %}<img src="{{ r.logoImg }}" alt="{{ r.name }}" class="h-6 mx-auto object-contain" loading="lazy">
                {%- elif r.logo %}<span class="{{ r.logo }} text-[20px] {{ 'text-flame' if r.bonfire else 'text-ink-2' }}" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="sr-only">{{ r.name }}</span>
                {%- elif r.logoChip %}<span class="inline-flex items-center justify-center bg-[#e9e4d6] rounded-[4px] p-[3px] mx-auto"><img src="{{ r.logoChip }}" alt="{{ r.name }}" class="h-[22px] w-[22px] object-contain grayscale" loading="lazy"></span><span class="sr-only">{{ r.name }}</span>
                {%- elif r.dom %}<span class="inline-flex items-center justify-center bg-[#e9e4d6] rounded-[4px] p-[3px] mx-auto"><img src="{{ r.dom | logo }}" alt="{{ r.name }}" class="h-[22px] w-[22px] object-contain" loading="lazy"></span><span class="sr-only">{{ r.name }}</span>
                {%- else %}<span class="font-disp font-[620] text-[.76rem] leading-[1.12] block {{ 'text-flame' if r.bonfire else 'text-ink' }}">{{ r.name }}</span>{% endif -%}
              </th>
              {%- endfor %}{%- endfor %}
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {# model / pricing — right under the platform names; detail on hover #}
            <tr class="hover:bg-ink/[0.02] border-b border-ink/[0.07]">
              <th class="{{ rowlabel }}">Model</th>
              {%- for g in groups %}{%- for r in g.rows %}
              <td title="{{ r.name }} · {{ r.model }}" class="px-1.5 py-2.5 text-center align-middle {{ 'border-l border-l-ink/20' if loop.first }} {{ stickyBonfireCell if r.bonfire }}">
                {%- if 'Nonprofit' in r.model and ('free' in r.model or 'AGPL' in r.model) -%}
                <span class="icon-[roentgen--free] text-flame text-[1.05rem] align-middle"></span> <span class="icon-[ph--hand-heart] text-flame text-[1.05rem] align-middle"></span>
                {%- else -%}
                {%- set paykey = 'nonprofit' if 'Nonprofit' in r.model else ('ads' if 'ad-funded' in r.model else ('freemium' if 'Freemium' in r.model else ('free' if ('AGPL' in r.model or 'GPL' in r.model or 'Free' in r.model) else 'paid'))) -%}
                <span class="{{ paymap[paykey] }} text-ink-3 text-[1.1rem] align-middle"></span>
                {%- endif -%}
                <span class="sr-only">{{ r.model }}</span>
              </td>
              {%- endfor %}{%- endfor %}
            </tr>
            {%- set bands = [{lab: "Ownership & openness", idx: [0,1,2,3,4,9]}, {lab: "Community features", idx: [5,6,7,8,10,11]}] %}
            {%- for band in bands %}
            <tr>
              <th class="sticky left-0 z-[2] bg-night-3 w-[150px] min-w-[150px] px-4 py-1.5 text-left font-smono text-[.56rem] font-bold tracking-[.14em] uppercase text-ink-3 border-y border-ink/[0.07]">{{ band.lab }}</th>
              <td colspan="99" class="bg-night-3/40 border-y border-ink/[0.07]"></td>
            </tr>
            {%- for i in band.idx %}
            <tr class="border-b border-ink/[0.07] hover:bg-ink/[0.02]">
              <th class="{{ rowlabel }}">{{ axes[i] }}</th>
              {%- for g in groups %}{%- for r in g.rows %}
              <td title="{{ r.name }} · {{ axes[i] }}: {{ {'yes':'Yes','no':'No','partial':'Partial','soon':'Coming'}[r.cells[i][0]] }}{% if r.cells[i][1] %} ({{ r.cells[i][1] }}){% endif %}" class="px-2 py-2.5 text-center {{ 'border-l border-l-ink/20' if loop.first }} {{ stickyBonfireCell if r.bonfire }}">{{ mark(r.cells[i][0], r.cells[i][2]) }}</td>
              {%- endfor %}{%- endfor %}
            </tr>
            {%- endfor %}
            {%- endfor %}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <p class="mt-4 font-smono text-[.66rem] text-ink-3 leading-[1.7] max-w-[70ch]">Scroll right for more platforms; hover any icon or platform for the detail behind it. Category-level and structural, as of 2026. Products within a category vary, and some span several. This isn't a scorecard of who's "best": Signal, the open-source forums, and mission-aligned projects like Roundabout and Acorn share many of our values with different tradeoffs. Spotted something wrong or out of date? <a class="text-spark hover:underline" href="/contact">Tell us and we'll fix it.</a> Already on the fediverse? The fediverse apps aren't here, because they answer a different question: <a class="text-spark hover:underline" href="/vs-mastodon">Mastodon vs Bonfire →</a><br><span class="inline-flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-4 gap-y-1 mt-2">Mobile app: <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1"><span class="icon-[ph--device-mobile-bold] text-leaf align-middle" aria-hidden="true"></span> your own branded app</span> <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1"><span class="icon-[ph--app-window-bold] text-leaf align-middle" aria-hidden="true"></span> one shared platform app</span> <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1"><span class="icon-[ph--stack-bold] text-leaf align-middle" aria-hidden="true"></span> an ecosystem of clients</span></span><br><span class="mt-2 inline-block">Icons via <a class="text-spark hover:underline" href="https://iconify.design" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Iconify</a>; logos via <a class="text-spark hover:underline" href="https://logo.dev" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Logo.dev</a>.</span></p>

    </div>
    </section>

    {# ---------- the honest version ---------- #}
    <section class="py-[clamp(56px,7vw,90px)] border-t border-ink/[0.07]" style="--acc:var(--color-corn)">
    <div class="max-w-[1140px] mx-auto px-7">
      <p class="{{ eyebrow }}"><i class="w-[9px] h-[9px] flex-none bg-[var(--acc)] [clip-path:polygon(50%_0,100%_50%,50%_100%,0_50%)]" aria-hidden="true"></i>What the table can't show</p>
      <h2 class="{{ display }}">The simple and honest facts.</h2>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 min-[821px]:grid-cols-3 gap-4 mt-9">
        <div class="{{ cell }}">
          <h3 class="{{ cellh }}">Open-source forums come closest</h3>
          <p class="{{ cellp }}">Discourse (with an ActivityPub plugin) and NodeBB (natively) even federate, and they're self-hostable and truly yours. A forum is a wonderful thing, but it's built around threads and categories. Bonfire brings that same ownership to a fuller shape: <b class="text-ink font-semibold">groups, circles, events, and decisions your community makes together</b>.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="{{ cell }}">
          <h3 class="{{ cellh }}">Federation is a work in progress, ours included</h3>
          <p class="{{ cellp }}">Bonfire's social layer federates across the fediverse today; <b class="text-ink font-semibold">group federation is still being built</b>, in the open with the <a href="https://github.com/swicg/groups/issues" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">W3C task force</a>. ATmosphere tools like Acorn and Roundabout hit the same wall, as ATproto has no cross-server group primitive yet.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="{{ cell }}">
          <h3 class="{{ cellh }}">The SaaS trade is convenience for control</h3>
          <p class="{{ cellp }}">Circle, Skool and Mighty are polished and quick to start, but your community lives on their platform, under their pricing, exportable only as far as they allow. Bonfire trades a little setup for a space that stays <a href="/mosaic">yours</a> for good.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    </section>

